{"url":"https://www.visitthecapitol.gov/visit/book-a-tour","title":"Book a Tour | U.S. Capitol - Visitor Center","description":"All tours, programs and activities are free of charge. Same day passes may be available, but reservations are recommended. Use our timed-entry ticketing system to select a day/time for a tour. ... <strong>Monday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m.</strong> Tuesday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Wednesday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m.","extra_snippets":["All tours are led by our professional tour guides and visit the Crypt, the Rotunda and National Statuary Hall. The tour route is subject to change. The tour does not include the Senate and House Galleries. Can I visit without a reservation? expand and show content · Same day passes may be available.","All tours, programs and activities are free of charge. Same day passes may be available, but reservations are recommended. Use our timed-entry ticketing system to select a day/time for a tour. ... Monday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Tuesday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Wednesday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m.","Thursday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Friday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Saturday: 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Sunday: closed The last tour of the day begins at 3:20 p.m. The Capitol Visitor Center is closed on Thanksgiving Day, Christmas Day, New Year's Day and Inauguration Day. What is included on the tour?","Attend a Specialty Tour, check out Exhibition Hall, peruse our Gift Shops or grab a bite to eat at our restaurant."]}
{"url":"https://sewardhouse.org/visit/tour-booking","title":"Tour Booking | Seward House Museum","description":"To book a tour for October 2026, ... avoid this fee, you can call us at (315) 252-1283 or purchase a ticket in person. Museum hours are <strong>Tuesday-Saturday from 10:00 AM - 5:00 PM</strong>....","extra_snippets":["General Info A guided tour is the only way to see the Museum. Tours begin at the top of the hour. Tour availability is subject to change. Sometimes we reach capacity due to large pre-scheduled groups. Advance reservations are available and advised. Visitors without pre-booked tickets will be admitted as capacity allows.","Tours run on the hour and the final tour of the day begins at 4:00 PM. Please see below for upcoming tour closures. The Museum is closed January through February and on most holidays. ... Up to ten cars can use the parking lot at the Museum. Overflow parking is availible at the Lincoln Street Parking Garage.","To book a tour for October 2026, please visit this page: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/seward-house-museum-tour-october-2026-ticke... Please be advised that our ticketing platform, Eventbrite, charges a small fee. To avoid this fee, you can call us at (315) 252-1283 or purchase a ticket in person. Museum hours are Tuesday-Saturday from 10:00 AM - 5:00 PM."]}
{"url":"https://tours.visitthecapitol.gov/","title":"Plan a Visit | U.S. Capitol Visitor Center","description":"Please enter value properly Some issue arise please try again Not enough pass(es) available ... 1.1 The Advance Reservation System (&quot;ARS&quot;) of the United States Capitol Visitor Center is a service provided to the public by the United States Congress to book reservations for tours of the United States Capitol.","extra_snippets":["Please enter value properly Some issue arise please try again Not enough pass(es) available ... 1.1 The Advance Reservation System (\"ARS\") of the United States Capitol Visitor Center is a service provided to the public by the United States Congress to book reservations for tours of the United States Capitol.","8. Cancellation of Your Tour of the United States Capitol · The U.S. Capitol reserves the right to suspend scheduled tours at any time and for any reason. To cancel your tour of the United States Capitol, please have your confirmation number available.","Q. How do I reserve a tour of the Capitol? A. Each person wishing to make a reservation must create an account in our reservation system. Please follow the instructions below to access the online reservation system. 1. Visit www.visitthecapitol.gov. 2. From the “Quick Links” menu, click “Book a Tour”, then select the option to “Book a Tour For Yourself”. (A new page will open.)","A. Visitors are able to cancel reserved tours via their account on the CVCs online reservation system. Please follow the instructions below to cancel reservations. 1. Visit www.visitthecapitol.gov. 2. From the “Quick Links” menu, click “Book a Tour”, then select the option to “Book a Tour for Yourself Online”. (A new page will open.)"]}
{"url":"https://azstateparks.com/kartchner/cave-tours/tours","title":"Cave Tour Information | Kartchner Caverns State Park","description":"All tours are led by a trained guide; no self-guided tours are available. Minors under age 18 are not permitted on tours without a parent or guardian. Various tours are scheduled daily. It is recommended that tours be booked as far in advance as possible to ensure availability.","extra_snippets":["All tours are led by a trained guide; no self-guided tours are available. Minors under age 18 are not permitted on tours without a parent or guardian. Various tours are scheduled daily. It is recommended that tours be booked as far in advance as possible to ensure availability.","Cave tour reservations are strongly encouraged. Please read through the information below in advance of your visit. The cave environment is unique and you may need to take special actions to prepare. Reserve online or call (877) MY-PARKS and select Option #2. You can call seven days a week, from 8 a.m.","Please arrive AT LEAST 30 minutes prior to your scheduled tour time. For tours starting at 8 a.m., please arrive at least 15 minutes early. Late arrival may result in the forfeiture of your reserved tour time.","This tour is available from October 15 to April 15 and is scheduled throughout the day. It is half of a mile long and takes an hour and 45 minutes to complete, one hour of which is underground. The Kartchner Cavern story is about amazing discoveries past, present, and future."]}
